&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and dynamic &lt;strong&gt;Delivery Transformation Director&lt;/strong&gt; to drive the successful execution and growth of large-scale transformation programs. The ideal candidate is a hands-on leader with a proven track record of delivering complex, large-scale projects at top-tier consulting firms. This is a unique opportunity to own the end-to-end delivery of our most strategic client engagements whilst shaping and expanding our solution and delivery capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Job responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-responsibilities content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the planning, execution, and delivery of complex transformation programs. Ensure projects are delivered on time, within budget, and to the highest quality standards, exceeding client expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Relationship Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Build and maintain strong, trusted relationships with C-level executives and key client stakeholders. Serve as the primary point of contact for all program-related matters and proactively manage risks and issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership and Program Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide mentorship and guidance to project teams, fostering a culture of excellence and accountability. Oversee resource allocation, project timelines, and budget management across multiple engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth and Business Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and pursue opportunities for program expansion and new business within existing accounts. Partner with the sales and solution teams to contribute to proposals, statements of work, and go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-qualifications&quot;&gt;Job qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-qualifications content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;professional-skills&quot;&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;skills inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of total professional experience, including 8+ years leading complex project delivery within a management consultancy, technology consulting firm, or digital engineering services company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in &lt;strong&gt;leading&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;delivering&lt;/strong&gt; multi-million-dollar, multi-year &lt;strong&gt;digital transformation&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;programs&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in &lt;strong&gt;managing fixed price and outcome based deliveries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional &lt;strong&gt;communication&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;presentation&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;skills&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to articulate complex &lt;strong&gt;technical concepts&lt;/strong&gt; to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;business&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;acumen&lt;/strong&gt; and a track record of driving &lt;strong&gt;business&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;growth&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;German&lt;/strong&gt; (B2/C1) required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;important-things&quot;&gt;Other things to know&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;important-things content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Work Modality&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hybrid (with up to 40% client-site travel)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no one-size-fits-all career path at Thoughtworks: however you want to develop your career is entirely up to you. But we also balance autonomy with the strength of our cultivation culture. This means your career is supported by interactive tools, numerous development programs and teammates who want to help you grow. We see value in helping each other be our best and that extends to empowering our employees in their career journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;responsible-ai-use&quot;&gt;Responsible Use of AI in Recruitment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;responsible-ai-use content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Thoughtworks, we use AI tools to support our recruitment team with administrative tasks such as drafting communications, scheduling interviews and writing job descriptions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Crucially, our AI tools do not screen, assess, rank or make hiring decisions. Every application is reviewed by our team and all selection decisions are made exclusively by our interviewers and hiring managers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to fairness and responsible AI. We actively manage our AI systems by testing, monitoring for biased outcomes and implementing mitigation measures. We hold our third-party vendors to these same high standards through a rigorous governance process. For additional information, please see our full &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks AI Policy for Recruitment&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about&quot;&gt;About Thoughtworks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;about content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thoughtworks is a dynamic and inclusive community of bright and supportive colleagues who are revolutionizing tech. As a leading technology consultancy, we’re pushing boundaries through our purposeful and impactful work. For 30+ years, we’ve delivered extraordinary impact together with our clients by helping them solve complex business problems with technology as the differentiator. Bring your brilliant expertise and commitment for continuous learning to Thoughtworks. Together, let’s be extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;display: none;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot;&gt;See here our AI policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics is a leading global sports platform redefining how fans connect with the teams, players and moments they love. Our businesses — Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, Fanatics Events, Fanatics Advertising, Fanatics Markets and Fanatics Studios — maximize the presence and reach for hundreds of partners globally and create a one-stop experience that allows fans to buy, bet, collect, and earn, while engaging with sports in deeper, more immersive ways. This includes licensed fan gear and lifestyle products, sportsbook and iGaming, physical and digital trading cards, live events, premium sports entertainment content, credit card offerings and more. Together, they form a powerful, integrated ecosystem — connected by the Fanatics ONE loyalty program and FanCash, the currency of sport — delivering personalized experiences to over 100 million fans worldwide. Fanatics holds partnerships with over 900 sports properties, from professional leagues and players’ associations to teams, colleges and retail partners; over 7,000 athletes and celebrities; and over 2,000 retail locations, including all Lids stores. Backed by a team of more than 22,000 employees, Fanatics is committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.organization-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launched in 2021, Fanatics Betting and Gaming is the online and retail sports betting subsidiary of Fanatics, a global digital sports platform. The Fanatics Sportsbook is available to 95% of the addressable online sports bettor market in the U.S. Fanatics Casino is currently available online in Michigan, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and West Virginia. Fanatics Betting and Gaming operates twenty-two retail sports betting locations, including the only sportsbook inside an NFL stadium at Northwest Stadium. Fanatics Betting and Gaming is headquartered in New York with offices in Denver, Leeds and Dublin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Campaign Operations Manager is a pivotal role responsible for taking operational delivery across CRM, Promotional Operations and Front-End Content &amp;amp; Merchandising to a new standard, giving the business and senior leadership genuine confidence in what&#39;s being built, executed and delivered across every owned channel and touchpoint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re hands on enough to troubleshoot live platforms and lead incident response the moment a campaign or promotion needs it, with an eagle-eyed view across everything live and everything coming next. You lead people the same way you lead delivery: coaching the team to raise their own standards, not just directing their work, and setting benchmarks the wider function can build on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating at the intersection of CRM, Operations and Product, this role is central to Fanatics&#39; ambition to become the #1 Online US Casino by 2030.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery Accountability &amp;amp; Operational Control&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold end-to-end accountability for the operational running of campaign, promotion and front end content delivery across the team, ensuring all requirements from Commercial, Analytics, Product and Engineering are in place from approved brief through build, QA, deployment, monitoring and post-launch review.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a complete, eagle-eyed view of delivery status, live risk and upcoming critical moments, keeping the campaign calendar, dependencies and escalation paths accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the team accountable for quality and timeliness, stepping in directly when delivery or player experience is at risk, and surfacing systemic risk that needs action beyond a single workstream.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Management &amp;amp; Operational Resilience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own on-call coverage and incident response for live campaigns, promotions and content, acting as the senior operational escalation point when delivery or execution risk surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot platform and execution issues hands on, coordinating containment, stakeholder communications, recovery and post incident follow up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own root-cause resolution, escalating platform-level causes to the CRM &amp;amp; Promotions Enablement Lead where needed and driving corrective action on recurring or high-severity incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the severity levels, playbooks and launch monitoring checklists that keep incident response consistent and repeatable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards, Governance &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set standards for campaign and content setup, audience selection, offer eligibility, testing, deployment and monitoring across owned channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational QA and release readiness gate that live activity must clear before launch, in partnership with Commercial, Legal, Compliance and Product, ensuring responsible gaming, privacy and jurisdictional requirements are met with clear audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the change controls, access permissions and documentation required for consistent, compliant and continuously improving execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Capability Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and develop the team, setting clear objectives, decision rights, performance expectations, and a benchmark for operational excellence that others are equipped to meet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build capability and confidence across the function through hands-on coaching, playbooks and structured knowledge sharing, rather than direction alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a culture of ownership and continuous improvement, where risks and mistakes are surfaced early and addressed constructively, and close capability or resourcing gaps as they emerge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CRM Planning on the campaign roadmap, upcoming plans and capacity signals so operational readiness is built in early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the critical interface into Customer Support and VIP, briefing them on upcoming activity, equipping them to resolve player escalations, and feeding recurring friction points back into delivery standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent operational readiness and delivery risk in cross functional planning for new campaigns, promotions, content and platform capabilities, connecting operational performance to player experience and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in CRM, campaign or promotional operations, delivery management or lifecycle marketing, including proven experience leading and developing a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountability for high-volume, time-sensitive operational delivery across multiple channels or workstreams in a complex digital consumer business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on working knowledge of CRM or promotional bonusing platforms (e.g. XtremePush, Braze, Optimove or similar) strong enough to troubleshoot live issues directly and assess technical risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading incident response, on-call governance or escalation frameworks for live activity, with sound operational judgement under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing or improving operational processes, controls, service levels and performance reporting, drawing on workflow management tools (e.g., Airtable, Jira).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent 360° stakeholder management and people leadership, able to influence senior stakeholders across CRM, Product, Compliance, Commercial, Legal, Customer Support and VIP while raising team capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in iGaming, sports betting or another regulated, compliance-heavy environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of online casino mechanics, bonusing platforms and player journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL or BI tools for operational diagnosis, reporting and performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in Agile or product-led delivery environments, and scaling operational governance or automation in a high-growth organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Ways of Working &amp;amp; Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Canada or UK based, hybrid role operating within Fanatics&#39; flexible working framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close partnership with both UK and US based teams, requiring effective collaboration across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional evening or weekend work during peak promotional periods and major campaign moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participation in a planned on-call rota is required, with on-call expectations and compensatory time managed in line with applicable local policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fanatics support a culture of trust and autonomy, enabling sustainable global collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, your interview and onboarding experience may include in-person components, such as onsite interviews or Launching into Better: LIVE—a multi-day cultural immersion in New York City for full-time, non-seasonal hires. These sessions are designed to build connection and bring our culture to life, though specific travel and participation requirements will be confirmed based on your role and location. Your recruiter will provide clear guidance at each stage of the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;PHENOGY AG is a leading innovator of battery energy storage technologies and solutions for the green electrification of the planet. Our team members work on future-proof and sustainable battery systems that are powerful, safe, and robust – with circularity as a central principle. Our technology partner network spans leading battery research institutes. PHENOGY is an environmentally and socially conscious enterprise. We are committed to fostering prosperity for the people and our planet, ensuring sustainable growth – starting in the area of our greatest expertise and impact: energy storage solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We energize the future.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;PHENOGY is seeking curious, entrepreneurial-minded energy pioneers to help shape our vision, systems, and growth; playing a key-role as we launch into our ambitious future. If you’re inspired by our mission, values, and drive to change how we energize the future — we’d love your application.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Purpose/Mission - The role owns the infrastructure, network and cybersecurity workstream for&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PHENOGY&#39;s corporate IT infrastructure (cloud, network, endpoints, identities and access) and its interfaces with the Battery Energy Storage System (BESS) product environment. It translates business, product, operational, customer and regulatory requirements into secure, resilient and auditable infrastructure and security controls across the BESS lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cybersecurity governance and the Information Security Management System (ISO/IEC 27001)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security architecture of BESS connectivity (EMS, BMS, gateways, IoT, APIs) and secure data exchange with partners such as Heidelberg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backup, business continuity and disaster recovery for critical systems (BESS/EMS, ERP, CRM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management of infrastructure and cybersecurity projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your Tasks &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as internal-facing and technical owner of the IT infrastructure and security landscape: network, firewalling and web filtering, Microsoft 365/Azure tenants, identity and access management, endpoints, backup, and secure remote/supplier access to BESS sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the asset and configuration inventory, network and security architecture documentation, risk register, vulnerability backlog, security policies and the infrastructure/security roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the risk management and vulnerability management cycle: periodic assessments, prioritisation, patching and remediation tracking across IT systems, applications, APIs and BESS connectivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and operate security monitoring, incident response, escalation paths, maintenance windows and problem management, together with external service providers (MSP/MSSP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define backup and retention policies (daily, monthly, yearly; 10+ years for critical data), offline/immutable backups, disaster-recovery runbooks and regular restore and DR tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define secure segmentation between corporate IT and the OT/BESS environment and secure remote access for O&amp;amp;M and field service, aligned with IEC 62443 concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide infrastructure, system-integration and cybersecurity support to the After Sales &amp;amp; Service framework once operational responsibility moves to the Service Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support B2B customer and audit requests: security questionnaires, tender requirements and compliance evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on when required: configure firewall rules, endpoint and identity policies, backup jobs and cloud security settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Projects (2027 portfolio)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Management &amp;amp; Vulnerability Assessment (Jan–Feb 2027): assess risks and vulnerabilities across all systems and deliver a prioritised remediation plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BESS Security Architecture II (Jan–Mar 2027): secure the BESS architecture and data exchange with Heidelberg, building on the current BESS security baseline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Continuity &amp;amp; Recovery System (Feb–Apr 2027): offline backup and disaster recovery for critical systems such as BESS/EMS, ERP and CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Improvements (Feb–Jun 2027): introduce firewalling and web filtering, which are not yet in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Threat Protection – ISO 27001 (Mar–May 2027): protect network and application traffic, including APIs and IP-based access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISO 27001 Enhancements (ongoing): close control gaps, maintain policies and evidence, and prepare for audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take over operation of granular backup and advanced endpoint management, and provide security input to the PHENOGY IoT solution POC (BMS/EMS communication and REST APIs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Core Competencies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead assigned infrastructure and cybersecurity projects from initiation through closure, using structured scope, schedule, budget, dependency, risk, issue, decision and change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create project charters, work breakdown structures, delivery plans, security requirements, test and DR-test plans, cutover plans, acceptance records and handover packages to operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate external suppliers (MSP/MSSP, network and firewall vendors, cloud providers, BESS/EMS partners) to resolve cross-functional blockers and escalate material decisions to the Head of IT and relevant governance bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide concise status reporting on progress, milestones, risk posture, vulnerabilities, incidents, suppliers and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree or equivalent professional experience in information technology, computer science, information security, engineering or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in IT infrastructure and cybersecurity management, including responsibility for delivering projects, ideally in an international mid-sized company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with network security (firewalls, VPN, segmentation, web filtering, IDS/IPS), Microsoft 365 / Entra ID / Intune / Defender, and backup and disaster recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running risk assessments, vulnerability management and security incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience implementing or maintaining an ISMS according to ISO/IEC 27001.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating technical suppliers and multidisciplinary stakeholders across business, IT and engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand operational technology and industrial-system boundaries without assuming ownership of safety engineering or embedded-control design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong documentation, risk management and executive-status reporting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional English; German or another relevant operating language is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strongly preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing Battery Energy Storage Systems, EMS, BMS, SCADA, PLC, PCS/inverters, industrial gateways, IoT or energy-data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of IEC 62443, NIS2 and the EU Cyber Resilience Act in mixed IT/OT environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Azure networking and security, Microsoft Sentinel / Defender XDR and enterprise firewall platforms (e.g. Fortinet, Palo Alto, Check Point).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with industrial protocols and secure integration patterns, including Modbus TCP, OPC UA, MQTT, REST APIs, API gateways and certificate/PKI management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with backup and DR solutions for cloud and hybrid environments, including immutable and offline backups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized credentials such as CISSP, CISM, ISO 27001 Lead Implementer/Auditor, GICSP, PMP, PRINCE2 or ITIL are advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decision-making authority: Approves infrastructure and security changes, firewall and access rules and security exceptions within the agreed policy framework and budget; may isolate systems or accounts during a security incident; escalates risk acceptance and major investments to the Head of IT.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting Line: Reporting to Head of IT Direct reports: none (functional lead of external infrastructure and security providers)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Workload: 100% - Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Travel: approx. 10% – PHENOGY offices, BESS customer sites and partner/supplier sites as required&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We offer you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Join a high-caliber environment that enables you to develop your full potential, shape your job, and take ownership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Participate in the development of PHENOGY and inspire the world to transition to sustainable energy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Become part of our eco-passionate expert team - a first-class team all around.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Benefit from flexible work hours as well as remote and on-site working in a modern sustainable office&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(26, 0, 120);&quot;&gt;Enjoy various events, an amazing coffee machine, and the occasional coffee from our CEO (acting Barista)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
